{
  "id": "COMPOUND:32553 - PROTEIN:6147",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential mechanism by which 6,7,3',4'-Tetramethoxyisoflavone may interact with Dehydrogenase/reductase SDR family member 9. This compound appears to target Microtubule-associated protein 1B, which is a known target of multiple flavonoids, including this compound. The subsequent pathways indicate that Microtubule-associated protein 1B is also a target of other compounds, such as 6-Hydroxy-2-[2-(2-hydroxyphenyl) ethyl]chromone and Oleamide, all of which are linked to the Dehydrogenase/reductase SDR family member 9. This suggests a possible convergent pathway where 6,7,3',4'-Tetramethoxyisoflavone may exert its effects through a shared mechanism involving the modulation of Microtubule-associated protein 1B, which in turn may influence the activity of SDR family member 9. The evidence is consistent with a mechanistic link, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be elucidated.",
